      "fTerm": "NEW PLANTS OR PROCESSES FOR OBTAINING THEM; PLANT REPRODUCTION BY TISSUE CULTURE TECHNIQUES<b>[5]</b><br><br><b><u>Note(s)</u></b><br><br><ul type=\"\"1\"\"><li>This subclass <u>covers</u> all aspects related to new plants, including disease resistance, cold resistance and growth speed.<b>[2018.01]</b></li><li>In this subclass, angiosperms, i.e. flowering plants, are classified in group <b>A01H 6/00</b> according to their botanic taxonomy and in group <b>A01H 5/00</b> according to their plant parts, where disclosed.</li></ul><br><br><b><u>Subclass indexes</u></b><br><table width=\"100%\"><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">PROCESSES</td><td><b>1/00</b>, <b>3/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">REPRODUCTION</td><td><b>4/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">FLOWERING PLANTS; GYMNOSPERMS</td><td><b>5/00</b>, <b>6/00</b>;<b>7/00</b></td></p></tr><tr><td width=\"70%\"><p style=\"\"text-indent:1em;margin:0\"\">OTHER PRODUCTS</td><td><b>9/00-17/00</b></td></p></tr></table>",
